      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The 300–1200 K regime concerns HfNbTaTiZr specimens containing 1 wt.% oxygen.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed model combines DFT calculations on oxygen-doped configurations with experimental electrical-conductivity data.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Machine-learning methods can learn useful predictive relationships for high-entropy materials from experimental datasets.",
