      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Impurity scattering and quantum localization may dominate conductivity in HfNbTaTiZr between 0 and 200 K.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Thermally activated conduction becomes significant in oxygen-doped HfNbTaTiZr between 300 and 1200 K.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10900490::web::013::structural_stability_of_lix_heo_at_high_",
        "PMC10900490::web::014::structural_stability_of_lix_heo_at_high_"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Carrier concentration and mobility can vary differently with temperature and jointly influence conductivity.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10900490::web::014::structural_stability_of_lix_heo_at_high_"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Existing analytical conductivity approaches assume defect-free crystals and therefore become inaccurate for oxygen-containing HfNbTaTiZr.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed model will closely match conductivity measurements in both the 0–200 K and 300–1200 K regimes.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At approximately 350 K, the 1 wt.% oxygen specimen will have an electrical conductivity of 1.2 ± 0.12 million S/m.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The model is applicable to bulk HfNbTaTiZr containing up to 1 wt.% oxygen.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reliable application is limited to 0–200 K for nearly perfect crystals and 300–1200 K for oxygen-doped specimens.",
